[7.481168, "o", "=== USTAR ===\r\n"]
[7.482388, "o", "ustar member header is 512 bytes. name occupies bytes 0-99. size octal occupies 124-135 (the slice end is 136). typeflag sits at 156: regular file uses ASCII 0 (the byte that Python writes as b\"0\"). Payload follows the header and is padded to 512.\r\n\r\nwalk_sig is hashlib.sha256 hex of regular-file names joined by newline in apply order (SHA-256). Length is 64. Alphabet is 0123456789abcdef.\r\n\r\nA quarry of truncated bytes or a non-ustar stream such as not-an-archive returns nonzero. A ledger filled with xxxx is junk and quarry must rebuild members.idx from the sealed kith.\r\n\r\npython3 -c import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(sys.stdin.buffer.read()).hexdigest())\r\n"]
[7.482711, "o", "=== DESK ===\r\n"]
[7.48378, "o", "Desk JSON keys: timezone, cluster, log_events, member_count, source_kith, walk_sig.\r\n\r\nsys.conf uses key=value lines. timezone and cluster come from the sys.conf payload the mill applies. log_events is the lexicographically sorted unique event strings from every app.log payload. member_count is the integer of regular-file payloads applied. source_kith is the archive basename.\r\n\r\nA brief archive copied to /tmp/kestrel.kith sits outside /app/sealwell. The sealed original also lives at /app/seed/sealwell/kestrel.kith.\r\n"]
[7.483962, "o", "=== APPLY ===\r\n"]
[7.484879, "o", "operator note: APPLY\r\n"]
[7.485035, "o", "=== SEAL ===\r\n"]
[7.486003, "o", "cordpit notes: two brief processes on one sealed kith must parse to one object. Paths outside sealwell fail.\r\n"]
[7.486206, "o", "=== TREE ===\r\n"]
[7.486987, "o", "idxmill\r\noverlaypit\r\nlogbag\r\nsiltcli\r\nustarwalk\r\ncfgbag\r\noffseturn\r\npaxcue\r\npidhash\r\nkeeppit\r\n"]
[7.487194, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bb15390b5ebf:/app# "]
